/**
 * @file StMtdSimMaker.dox
 * @brief Doxygen documentation for the STAR MTD Simulation Maker.
 *
 * This file contains the full Doxygen narrative, group definition, and
 * per-method documentation for StMtdSimMaker.  It is intended to be
 * picked up by the Doxyfile in the same directory; no changes to the
 * source headers are required.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @defgroup StMtdSim MTD Simulation (StMtdSimMaker)
 * @brief Monte-Carlo simulation of the STAR Muon Telescope Detector (MTD).
 *
 * @section mtdsim_overview Overview
 *
 * The Muon Telescope Detector (MTD) is an MRPC (Multi-gap Resistive Plate
 * Chamber) based detector installed on the outer face of the STAR magnet
 * return yoke at a radius of approximately 403 cm.  Its primary physics goal
 * is the identification of muons produced in heavy-ion and p+p collisions,
 * enabling studies of charmonium (J/ψ, ψ') and upsilon (Υ) production via
 * their di-muon decay channels, as well as direct muon measurements.
 *
 * @section mtdsim_geometry Detector Geometry
 *
 * The MTD is organised hierarchically:
 *
 * | Level      | Name      | Count (typical) | Description                          |
 * |------------|-----------|-----------------|--------------------------------------|
 * | Backleg    | backleg   | up to 30        | Large structural unit on yoke sector |
 * | Module     | module    | 1–5 per backleg | Individual MRPC tray                 |
 * | Cell       | cell      | 12 per module   | Single strip/pad (read-out channel)  |
 *
 * Each module houses 12 readout cells (strips) of width
 * @f$ w_{\rm pad} = 38\,\mathrm{mm} + 6\,\mathrm{mm} = 44\,\mathrm{mm} @f$
 * (active pad plus inner dead zone).
 *
 * Because physical backleg numbering does not match the GEANT volume numbering,
 * a database-resident mapping table (@c mtdGeant2BacklegIDMap) is loaded at
 * the start of each run and used to translate GEANT backleg indices to the
 * hardware backleg IDs stored in reconstructed hits.
 *
 * @section mtdsim_readout Readout and Channel Mapping
 *
 * Each cell is read out from @e both ends of the strip (West and East),
 * providing two TDC leading-edge times, @f$ t_W @f$ and @f$ t_E @f$, and
 * two trailing-edge times separated by a fixed time-over-threshold (TOT) of
 * 15 ns.  The signal propagation velocity along the strip is
 * @f$ v = 56\,\mathrm{ps/cm} @f$.  For a hit at local longitudinal coordinate
 * @f$ z @f$ (in cm) and true time of flight @f$ t_{\rm TOF} @f$:
 *
 * @f[
 *   t_W = t_{\rm TOF} - z \cdot v, \qquad
 *   t_E = t_{\rm TOF} + z \cdot v
 * @f]
 *
 * The channel number on the RDO (Readout Data Object) is derived from a
 * 5-module × 24-cell lookup table @c mModuleChannel.  Two consecutive RDO
 * channel numbers are assigned per cell: @c channel1 (West/leading) and
 * @c channel2 = @c channel1 + 12 (East/leading).
 *
 * @section mtdsim_timing Timing Resolution
 *
 * The intrinsic time resolution of the MTD MRPC is modelled as a Gaussian
 * smear with @f$ \sigma_t = 99\,\mathrm{ps} @f$ applied to the GEANT
 * time-of-flight:
 *
 * @f[
 *   t_{\rm sim} = t_{\rm GEANT} + \mathcal{N}(0,\,\sigma_t)
 * @f]
 *
 * The smeared time is stored in the @c StMtdHit via the leading-edge pair.
 *
 * @section mtdsim_cellid Cell-ID Encoding
 *
 * A unique integer cell ID encodes the full detector address as
 * @f[
 *   \mathrm{cellId} = \mathrm{icell} + 100\cdot(\mathrm{imodule} + 100\cdot\mathrm{ibackleg})
 * @f]
 * This encoding is used as the key in the per-event @c std::map that
 * accumulates hits and resolves multiple GEANT steps in the same cell (only
 * the latest step by time-of-flight is retained).
 *
 * @section mtdsim_workflow Processing Workflow
 *
 * @code{.unparsed}
 *   InitRun()
 *     └─ load mtdGeant2BacklegIDMap from STAR database
 *     └─ initialise mModuleChannel[5][24] sequential channel map
 *
 *   Make()  [called once per event]
 *     └─ retrieve g2t_mtd_hit table from GEANT dataset
 *     └─ call FastCellResponse()
 *           └─ for each GEANT step:
 *                 CalcCellId()  →  ibackleg, imodule, icell, cellId
 *                 apply 99 ps Gaussian timing smear
 *                 compute leadingW, leadingE, trailingW, trailingE
 *                 fill QA histograms
 *                 store StMtdHit in std::map (latest tof wins)
 *           └─ add all StMtdHit objects to StMtdCollection in StEvent
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section mtdsim_qa Quality-Assurance Histograms
 *
 * When @c mBookHisto is @c kTRUE (default), the following ROOT histograms
 * are booked in @c bookHistograms() and may be written to @c mtdsim.root
 * when @c mWriteHisto is @c kTRUE:
 *
 * | Histogram         | Type  | Description                                      |
 * |-------------------|-------|--------------------------------------------------|
 * | @c QABacklegChannel | TH2I | MTD hit distribution: backleg vs RDO channel    |
 * | @c DeGeant        | TH1F  | Deposited energy from GEANT step (keV)           |
 * | @c TofGeant       | TH1F  | True time of flight from GEANT (ns)              |
 * | @c DeSeen         | TH1F  | Deposited energy after cell response             |
 * | @c TofSeen        | TH1F  | Smeared time of flight after cell response (ns)  |
 * | @c TofResSeen     | TH1F  | Timing residual after detector response (ps)     |
 * | @c TofResReco     | TH1F  | Timing residual after reconstruction (ps)        |
 * | @c ADCReco        | TH1F  | ADC spectrum (currently unfilled placeholder)    |
 * | @c TDCReco        | TH1F  | TDC spectrum                                     |
 * | @c TACorr         | TH2F  | Time–amplitude slewing correlation               |
 * | @c ModuleHist     | TH1F  | Module index distribution                        |
 * | @c mBetaHist      | TH1F  | Particle velocity β                              |
 * | @c mPathLHist     | TH1F  | Track path length (cm)                           |
 * | @c mTofHist       | TH1F  | Total time of flight (ns)                        |
 * | @c mRecMass       | TH1F  | Reconstructed particle mass (GeV/c²)             |
 *
 * @section mtdsim_references References
 *
 * - L. Ruan et al., "Perspectives for the study of J/ψ via dimuon channel at
 *   RHIC", J. Phys. G 36 (2009) 025001.
 * - STAR MTD Technical Design Report (BNL internal, 2012).
 * - B. Bonner et al., "A single-gap resistive-plate-chamber time-of-flight
 *   detector for STAR", Nucl. Instrum. Meth. A 508 (2003) 181.
 *
 * @author Frank Geurts
 * @author Yi Yang (yiyang@bnl.gov) — 2014 updates
 * @author Alex Jentsch — geometry mapping corrections (2013–2014)
 * @author Bill LLope — name-clash fix (2014)
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @class StMtdSimMaker
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief STAR maker that converts GEANT MTD hits into reconstructed-level
 *        @c StMtdHit objects stored in an @c StMtdCollection.
 *
 * StMtdSimMaker sits in the standard STAR BFC (Big Full Chain) maker sequence
 * between the GEANT simulation step and the reconstruction makers.  It reads
 * the @c g2t_mtd_hit table produced by GEANT and, for each valid hit:
 *
 * -# decodes the GEANT volume identifier into a physical (backleg, module,
 *    cell) address via CalcCellId();
 * -# applies a 99 ps Gaussian timing smear;
 * -# computes dual-end leading and trailing TDC times using the known signal
 *    propagation velocity along the strip;
 * -# packages the result as an @c StMtdHit and appends it to the
 *    @c StMtdCollection attached to the current @c StEvent.
 *
 * @note Only one GEANT step per cell is retained per event.  If multiple
 *       steps deposit energy in the same cell, the step with the
 *       @e largest time of flight is kept (last step wins).
 *
 * @note Hit association to the Monte-Carlo track (@c idTruth) is set with
 *       100 % quality; track association to reconstructed tracks is deferred
 *       to @c StMtdMatchMaker.
 *
 * @par Typical usage in a BFC macro:
 * @code
 *   StMtdSimMaker *mtdSim = new StMtdSimMaker("MtdSim");
 *   chain->AddMaker(mtdSim);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @par Controlling output:
 * @code
 *   mtdSim->mBookHisto  = kTRUE;   // book QA histograms (default: true)
 *   mtdSim->mWriteHisto = kTRUE;   // write mtdsim.root at end of job
 * @endcode
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Constructor
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn StMtdSimMaker::StMtdSimMaker(const char *name)
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Constructs the maker and initialises all data members to safe defaults.
 *
 * All ROOT histogram pointers and GEANT data pointers are set to @c nullptr.
 * The @c mModuleChannel lookup table is zeroed via @c memset.  Default
 * control flags are:
 *   - @c mBookHisto  = @c kTRUE  — QA histograms are booked in Init().
 *   - @c mWriteHisto = @c kFALSE — histograms are @e not written at Finish().
 *   - @c mWriteStEvent = @c kTRUE — simulated hits are written into @c StEvent.
 *   - @c mHistFile  = @c "mtdsim.root".
 *
 * @c Reset() is called at the end of construction to zero event-level pointers.
 *
 * @param[in] name  Maker name registered with the STAR framework.
 *                  Defaults to @c "MtdSim".  Must differ from the BTof
 *                  maker name (@c "TofSim") to avoid chain name clashes.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Destructor
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn StMtdSimMaker::~StMtdSimMaker()
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Destructor.  No heap resources are owned by this class; ROOT manages
 *        histogram lifetime via gDirectory/TFile ownership.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Reset
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn void StMtdSimMaker::Reset()
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Resets event-level pointers in preparation for the next event.
 *
 * Sets @c mGeantData and @c mEvent to @c nullptr.  If @c mWriteStEvent is
 * @c kTRUE, also deletes the current @c StMtdCollection (the collection
 * will be re-created and attached to the new @c StEvent in
 * @c FastCellResponse()).
 *
 * This method is called automatically from the constructor and may be called
 * explicitly between events if needed.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Init
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn virtual Int_t StMtdSimMaker::Init()
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Framework initialisation called once before the first event.
 *
 * If @c mBookHisto is @c kTRUE, calls @c bookHistograms() to allocate all
 * QA ROOT histograms.  Then delegates to @c StMaker::Init() which handles
 * registration with the chain.
 *
 * @return @c kStOK on success; propagates any error from @c StMaker::Init().
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// InitRun
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn Int_t StMtdSimMaker::InitRun(Int_t runnumber)
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Run-level initialisation called once per run number.
 *
 * Performs two initialisation tasks:
 *
 * **1. GEANT-to-hardware backleg ID map (database)**
 *
 * Queries the STAR offline database path
 * @c Geometry/mtd/mtdGeant2BacklegIDMap for the @c mtdGeant2BacklegIDMap
 * table, which contains 30 integer entries mapping GEANT backleg indices
 * (1–30) to physical hardware backleg IDs.  The result is stored in the
 * module-level array @c geant2backlegIDMap[30].
 *
 * If the table is not found in the database the method returns @c kStErr
 * and logs an error via @c LOG_ERROR.
 *
 * **2. RDO channel map**
 *
 * Fills @c mModuleChannel[5][24] with sequential channel numbers 1–120,
 * where @c mModuleChannel[module][cell] gives the first (West) RDO channel
 * for that module/cell pair.  The East channel is always
 * @c mModuleChannel[module][cell] + 12.
 *
 * @param[in] runnumber  STAR run number (used implicitly by @c GetDataBase
 *                       to select the correct database snapshot).
 * @return @c kStOK on success, @c kStErr if the database table is missing.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FinishRun
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn Int_t StMtdSimMaker::FinishRun(Int_t runnumber)
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Run-level teardown called once per run.  Currently a no-op.
 *
 * @param[in] runnumber  STAR run number (unused).
 * @return @c kStOk.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Make
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn virtual Int_t StMtdSimMaker::Make()
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Main per-event processing method called by the STAR framework.
 *
 * Execution sequence:
 *
 * -# Retrieve the GEANT dataset from the input chain, trying both the
 *    @c "geant" branch (BFC chain) and the @c "geantBranch" branch
 *    (standalone GEANT file reading).  If neither is present, returns
 *    @c kStWarn.
 * -# Find the @c g2t_mtd_hit table in the GEANT dataset.  Returns
 *    @c kStWarn if the table is absent or empty.
 * -# Cache the pointer to the @c StEvent currently in the chain
 *    (may be @c nullptr for GEANT-only running).
 * -# Call @c FastCellResponse() to convert GEANT steps to @c StMtdHit
 *    objects and populate @c StMtdCollection.
 *
 * @return @c kStOK on success, @c kStWarn if no GEANT data or MTD hits
 *         are found.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Finish
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn virtual Int_t StMtdSimMaker::Finish()
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief End-of-job cleanup called by the framework after all events.
 *
 * If @c mWriteHisto is @c kTRUE, opens the ROOT file named by @c mHistFile
 * (default @c "mtdsim.root") in RECREATE mode, calls @c writeHistograms()
 * to flush all QA histograms, then closes the file.
 *
 * @return @c kStOK.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FastCellResponse
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn Int_t StMtdSimMaker::FastCellResponse()
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Core simulation routine: converts GEANT MTD hits to @c StMtdHit
 *        objects with realistic timing and stores them in @c StMtdCollection.
 *
 * This is the heart of the MTD simulation.  It iterates over all GEANT steps
 * cached in @c mMtdHitsFromGeant and, for each step with positive track length
 * (@c s_track > 0) and positive energy deposit (@c de > 0):
 *
 * **Step 1 — Geometry decoding**
 *
 * Calls CalcCellId() with the GEANT @c volume_id and the local Y coordinate
 * @c ghit.x[1] to obtain @c ibackleg, @c imodule, @c icell, and the
 * packed @c cellId integer.  Hits with invalid cell IDs (@c cellId < 0) are
 * skipped.
 *
 * **Step 2 — Hit deduplication**
 *
 * A @c std::map<int,StMtdHit*> keyed by @c cellId accumulates hits.  If a
 * hit already exists for that cell, the @e later GEANT step (larger
 * @c ghit.tof) is kept and the earlier is discarded.  This models the
 * last-step-wins behaviour of a triggered detector.
 *
 * **Step 3 — Timing simulation**
 *
 * The true time of flight @c ghit.tof (in GEANT time units, converted to
 * nanoseconds) is smeared by a Gaussian random deviate with
 * @f$ \sigma = 99\,\mathrm{ps} @f$ drawn from a Ranlux-engine-based
 * generator:
 * @f[
 *   t_{\rm sim} = t_{\rm GEANT} + \mathcal{N}(0,\,99\,\mathrm{ps})
 * @f]
 *
 * **Step 4 — Leading/trailing edge calculation**
 *
 * The signal propagation velocity along the strip is
 * @f$ v = 56\times10^{-3}\,\mathrm{ns/cm} @f$.
 * Using the longitudinal local coordinate @c ghit.x[2] (in cm):
 * @f{align}{
 *   t_{W,\rm lead}  &= t_{\rm GEANT} - z \cdot v \\
 *   t_{E,\rm lead}  &= t_{\rm GEANT} + z \cdot v \\
 *   t_{W,\rm trail} &= t_{W,\rm lead} + 15\,\mathrm{ns} \\
 *   t_{E,\rm trail} &= t_{E,\rm lead} + 15\,\mathrm{ns}
 * @f}
 *
 * The 15 ns trailing offset corresponds to a fixed time-over-threshold.
 *
 * **Step 5 — StMtdHit population**
 *
 * The following fields of @c StMtdHit are set:
 *   - @c backleg (hardware backleg ID)
 *   - @c module  (module index within backleg)
 *   - @c cell    (cell index, 0–11)
 *   - @c leadingEdgeTime  = @f$(t_{W,\rm lead},\, t_{E,\rm lead})@f$
 *   - @c trailingEdgeTime = @f$(t_{W,\rm trail},\, t_{E,\rm trail})@f$
 *   - @c associatedTrack = @c NULL (assigned later by StMtdMatchMaker)
 *   - @c idTruth (GEANT track index @c ghit.track_p, quality = 100 %)
 *
 * **Step 6 — StMtdCollection**
 *
 * After all GEANT steps are processed, the unique @c StMtdHit objects from
 * the map are added to the @c StMtdCollection of the current @c StEvent
 * (creating a new collection if none exists).  If no @c StEvent is available,
 * a standalone @c StMtdCollection is created.
 *
 * @return @c kStOK.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CalcCellId
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn Int_t StMtdSimMaker::CalcCellId(Int_t volume_id, Float_t ylocal, Int_t &ibackleg, Int_t &imodule, Int_t &icell)
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Decodes a GEANT volume identifier and local Y coordinate into a
 *        physical MTD detector address.
 *
 * The GEANT volume ID encodes geometry hierarchically.  The decoding scheme
 * is:
 * @code
 *   ires        = volume_id / 100
 *   backlegTemp = ires / 10           // GEANT backleg index (1-based)
 *   imodule     = ires % 10           // module within backleg (1-based)
 * @endcode
 *
 * The physical hardware backleg ID is obtained by looking up @c backlegTemp
 * (decremented by 1 for 0-based indexing) in @c geant2backlegIDMap[]:
 * @code
 *   ibackleg = geant2backlegIDMap[backlegTemp - 1]
 * @endcode
 *
 * **Module number correction for backlegs 12–20:**
 * Backlegs 12–20 are on a sector of the magnet yoke where the module
 * enumeration starts at 2 rather than 1.  For these backlegs, @c imodule
 * is incremented by 1.
 *
 * **Cell index from local Y:**
 * The local Y coordinate of the hit (in cm) is converted to a cell index
 * using the pad pitch:
 * @f[
 *   \mathrm{icell} = \left\lfloor
 *     \frac{y_{\rm local} + w_{\rm pad}\cdot N_{\rm cell}/2}{w_{\rm pad}}
 *   \right\rfloor
 * @f]
 * where @f$ w_{\rm pad} = 4.4\,\mathrm{cm} @f$ and @f$ N_{\rm cell} = 12 @f$.
 *
 * **Cell orientation flip for modules > 3:**
 * For modules with index > 3 the cell numbering runs in the opposite
 * direction, so the index is mirrored:
 * @code
 *   if (imodule > 3) icell = 11 - icell;
 * @endcode
 *
 * **Range validation:**
 * | Condition                              | Return value |
 * |----------------------------------------|--------------|
 * | @c ibackleg < 0 or > @c kNBackleg (99) | -3           |
 * | @c imodule  < 0 or > @c kNModule  (99) | -2           |
 * | @c icell    < 0 or ≥ @c kNCell    (12) | -1           |
 * | All valid                              | encoded cell ID ≥ 0 |
 *
 * **Packed cell ID encoding:**
 * @f[
 *   \mathrm{cellId} = \mathrm{icell} + 100\cdot(\mathrm{imodule}
 *                     + 100\cdot\mathrm{ibackleg})
 * @f]
 *
 * @param[in]  volume_id  GEANT volume identifier from @c g2t_mtd_hit_st.
 * @param[in]  ylocal     Local Y coordinate of the hit in cm
 *                        (@c ghit.x[1] in the GEANT hit structure).
 * @param[out] ibackleg   Hardware backleg ID (1-based) after database mapping.
 * @param[out] imodule    Module index within the backleg (1-based).
 * @param[out] icell      Cell index within the module (0-based, 0–11).
 * @return Packed cell ID ≥ 0 on success; negative error code on failure
 *         (-1: bad cell, -2: bad module, -3: bad backleg).
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// bookHistograms
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn Int_t StMtdSimMaker::bookHistograms()
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Allocates all QA ROOT histograms used by the simulation.
 *
 * Called from Init() when @c mBookHisto is @c kTRUE.  All histograms are
 * owned by the current ROOT directory (typically the framework's in-memory
 * file).  The following histograms are created:
 *
 * **Kinematic / tracking QA**
 * | Name           | Bins / Range            | Description                  |
 * |----------------|-------------------------|------------------------------|
 * | @c mBetaHist   | 100 bins, [−2, 2]       | Particle velocity β          |
 * | @c mPathLHist  | 100 bins, [−2, 500] cm  | Track path length            |
 * | @c mTofHist    | 1000 bins, [−10, 10000] ns | Total time of flight      |
 * | @c mRecMass    | 1000 bins, [−2, 4] GeV  | Reconstructed mass           |
 *
 * **GEANT-level MTD**
 * | Name           | Bins / Range            | Description                  |
 * |----------------|-------------------------|------------------------------|
 * | @c mCellGeant  | 2-D, cell vs module     | Cell ID of GEANT hit         |
 * | @c mNCellGeant | 2-D, cell vs module     | Number of cells per GEANT hit|
 * | @c mDeGeant    | 1000 bins, [0, 10] keV  | Energy deposit               |
 * | @c mTofGeant   | 1000 bins, [0, 20] ns   | True time of flight          |
 *
 * **After detector response**
 * | Name            | Bins / Range             | Description                 |
 * |-----------------|--------------------------|------------------------------|
 * | @c mCellSeen    | 2-D, cell vs module      | Cell ID after response       |
 * | @c mNCellSeen   | 2-D                      | Cell multiplicity            |
 * | @c mDeSeen      | 1000 bins, [0, 10] keV   | Energy deposit               |
 * | @c mT0Seen      | 1000 bins, [0, 20] ns    | Start-time estimate          |
 * | @c mTofSeen     | 1000 bins, [0, 20] ns    | Smeared time of flight       |
 * | @c mTofResSeen  | 1001 bins, [−500, 500] ps| Timing residual (detector)   |
 *
 * **After reconstruction**
 * | Name             | Bins / Range             | Description                 |
 * |------------------|--------------------------|------------------------------|
 * | @c mCellReco     | 2-D, cell vs module      | Cell ID after reconstruction |
 * | @c mNCellReco    | 2-D                      | Cell multiplicity            |
 * | @c mADCReco      | 4096 bins, [0, 4096]     | ADC spectrum (placeholder)   |
 * | @c mTDCReco      | 4096 bins, [0, 4096]     | TDC spectrum                 |
 * | @c mT0Reco       | 1000 bins, [0, 20] ns    | Reconstructed start time     |
 * | @c mTofResReco   | 1000 bins, [−300, 300] ps| Timing residual (reco)       |
 * | @c mTACorr       | 512×512, TDC vs ADC      | Time-amplitude slewing       |
 *
 * **Occupancy**
 * | Name               | Bins / Range                 | Description              |
 * |--------------------|------------------------------|--------------------------|
 * | @c mModHist        | 201 bins, [−100, 100]        | Module index             |
 * | @c QABacklegChannel | 30×120 (backleg × channel)  | Hit occupancy map        |
 *
 * @return @c kStOk.
 */

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// writeHistograms
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @fn Int_t StMtdSimMaker::writeHistograms()
 * @ingroup StMtdSim
 * @brief Writes all booked QA histograms to the currently open ROOT file.
 *
 * Called from Finish() when @c mWriteHisto is @c kTRUE, after the output
 * file has been opened and @c cd()'d into.  Calls @c TH1::Write() /
 * @c TH2::Write() on every histogram pointer.  No null-pointer checks are
 * performed; the caller must ensure @c bookHistograms() was called first.
 *
 * @return @c kStOk.
 */
